## 27. Acceptance Criteria

The project is considered functionally complete only when the following scenario works in the local demo environment:

A citizen opens CivicPulse AI, selects Tamil or English, creates an account, submits a complaint with a description and location, and receives a reference number.

The backend analyzes the complaint, identifies the appropriate configured department using category and jurisdiction rules, and explains the routing decision.

If the responsible authority is uncertain, the complaint is placed in a review queue rather than routed arbitrarily.

The complaint is sent through a configured delivery adapter. Its actual delivery result and any retry attempts are stored.

The citizen can see whether the complaint is awaiting routing, delivered to the configured destination, awaiting acknowledgement, acknowledged, or experiencing a delivery failure.

The authority dashboard displays the same complaint, its routing decision, delivery history, acknowledgement history, and deadlines.

The system can demonstrate a missed acknowledgement deadline, a permitted escalation, a notification, a resolution update, and citizen verification.

All status changes and important actions are recorded in the audit history.

The full demonstration workflow must function without real government credentials by using a clearly labelled mock authority adapter. Production delivery to an external government authority must remain dependent on a verified, authorized integration.

